    {
      "id": "tour:hmr",
      "title": "How Vite chooses a hot update or reload",
      "summary": "A Vite development server watches changed files and checks which loaded modules they affect. An accepting module can receive a targeted hot update. A dead end in the importer chain or a client HTML template change triggers a page reload. This guide follows that choice and the message sent to the browser.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "view": "view:hmr",
          "focus": [
            "hmr:1"
          ],
          "note": "### A changed file starts a boundary search\n\nThe server forwards changed files to the update handler. For each affected environment, the handler passes matched modules to the update decision.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/index.ts",
              "find": "await handleHMRUpdate(type, file, server)",
              "role": "call-site"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/vite/src/node/server/hmr.ts",
              "symbol": "handleHMRUpdate",
